{
  "schemaVersion": "tl-rewrite.counterexample-corpus/v1",
  "purpose": "The counterevidence corpus. Every case is a formula pair whose bounded comparison must reach a declared outcome, and every mismatch case must yield a concrete counterexample trace that is independently replayed against both documents. A counterexample that has degraded into a boolean is the failure this corpus exists to prevent.",
  "oracle": "The counts and per-case expectations in this file are the oracle. The producer reads them, runs the comparison, and reports what it observed; the chain compares observed counts against the counts declared here rather than against the producer's own output, so a producer that stopped finding counterexamples cannot also move the number it is checked against.",
  "counts": {
    "mismatch": 5,
    "non_conclusive": 5,
    "malformed": 1,
    "total": 11
  },
  "unavailableIsNotACase": "There is deliberately no absent-input case here. A declared input that is missing makes the proof genuinely unavailable, and wiring a permanently unavailable case into the green path would either wedge the gate red or teach the mapping to read unavailable as a pass. The state is demonstrated instead by a chain scenario that seals an `unavailable` attestation, and the producer's ability to report it is demonstrated by a mutation probe that removes a declared input and requires the row and the proof to go unavailable.",
